Feature: Masking last 4 digits of invoice numbers in d_product_revenue table

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog purgo_playground.d_product_revenue exists
    And data backup procedures have been confirmed
    And validation and testing criteria for masked data are established

  Scenario: Create masked invoice_number in replica table
    Given the table d_product_revenue_clone does not exist
    When I create a replica of d_product_revenue table as d_product_revenue_clone
    Then d_product_revenue_clone should have the same schema as d_product_revenue

  Scenario Outline: Mask last 4 digits of invoice_number
    Given the invoice_number "<original_invoice>"
    When I apply masking logic using PySpark to mask last 4 digits
    Then the invoice_number should be "<masked_invoice>"

    Examples:
      | original_invoice | masked_invoice  |
      | 1234234534      | 123423****       |
      | 9876543210      | 987654****       |

  Scenario: Error when masking on non-string invoice_number
    Given the invoice_number data type is not a string
    When I attempt to perform masking
    Then an error message should be "Invalid data type for invoice_number. Expected string."

  Scenario: Validate masked data in d_product_revenue_clone
    Given the masked invoice_number values are in place
    When I query the replica table d_product_revenue_clone
    Then all invoice_number values should conform to the masking format "******<last 4 digits masked>"

  Scenario: Performance test for large data volume
    Given the data volume exceeds 10 million rows
    When I execute the masking logic
    Then the processing time should not exceed 5 minutes

  Scenario: Restoration after drop fails
    Given the table d_product_revenue_clone was dropped
    And backup files exist for restoration
    When I trigger the restore process
    Then d_product_revenue_clone should be restored successfully without data loss

  Scenario: Error scenario for dropping non-existent table
    Given the table d_product_revenue_clone does not exist
    When I attempt to drop d_product_revenue_clone
    Then an error message should be "Table d_product_revenue_clone does not exist."
